From: rn212-debian
Subject: [PATCH] ata: ahci: force port map on Annapurna Labs Alpine AHCI

The Alpine internal AHCI (1c36:0031) reports AHCI 1.3 with PORTS_IMPL = 0.
Since mainline only fabricates a port map for AHCI < 1.3, all four ports
come up as DUMMY and the ReadyNAS RN212 bay disks (ata1/ata2 on stock) are
never seen. The stock 4.x kernel logs "forcing PORTS_IMPL to 0xf" here.
---
--- a/drivers/ata/ahci.c
+++ b/drivers/ata/ahci.c
@@ -773,6 +773,17 @@
 	}
 
 	/*
+	 * The Alpine SoC AHCI reports AHCI 1.3 with PORTS_IMPL = 0, so libahci
+	 * no longer fabricates a port map for it and every port ends up DUMMY.
+	 * Force all 4 ports, as the stock ReadyNAS kernel does.
+	 */
+	if (pdev->vendor == PCI_VENDOR_ID_AMAZON_ANNAPURNA_LABS &&
+	    pdev->device == 0x0031) {
+		dev_info(&pdev->dev, "Alpine AHCI: forcing port_map 0xf\n");
+		hpriv->saved_port_map = 0xf;
+	}
+
+	/*
 	 * Temporary Marvell 6145 hack: PATA port presence
 	 * is asserted through the standard AHCI port
 	 * presence register, as bit 4 (counting from 0)
